=========================================================
   OVERVIEW: display: none
   =========================================================

Definition:
display: none completely removes an element from the page layout.
The element is not visible and does not occupy any space.

---------------------------------------------------------
WHAT HAPPENS WHEN display: none IS USED
---------------------------------------------------------
- Element is not rendered on the page
- Element takes up NO space
- Other elements behave as if it does not exist
- Width, height, margin, and padding have no effect

---------------------------------------------------------
display: none vs visibility: hidden
---------------------------------------------------------
display: none
- Element is removed from layout
- No space is reserved

visibility: hidden
- Element is invisible
- Space is still reserved

---------------------------------------------------------
COMMON USE CASES
---------------------------------------------------------
- Hiding elements temporarily
- Showing/hiding content using JavaScript
- Responsive design (hide elements on small screens)
- Debugging layouts

---------------------------------------------------------
IMPORTANT NOTE
---------------------------------------------------------
An element with display: none cannot be focused or interacted with.
It is completely removed from the document flow.
